title: How to Stop Him
subtitle: The Jedi are going to move against the Chancellor. How?
tags: event
view-if: finale and not gambit and finale_day >= 5 and sidious_known and not arrest_plan_seen
max-visits: 1
priority: 10
new-page: true
face-image: img/ev_jedi.svg
on-arrival: arrest_plan_seen = 1

= How to Stop Him

Master Windu and three Jedi Masters intend to arrest the Chancellor today. Windu wants the Senate with him. [? if warrant : The sealed warrant prepared by the Judiciary Committee is ready. ?][? if not warrant : There is no warrant. The Jedi would be acting on their own authority. ?]

- @warrant: Arrest him with the Senate's warrant.
- @emergency_warrant: Rush an emergency warrant through the Supreme Court.
- @expose: Expose him before the full Senate first.
- @jedi: Let the Jedi act alone, now, before he can react.

@warrant
view-if: warrant
subtitle: The arrest will be lawful.
on-arrival: arrest_mode = "warrant"; arrest_planned = 1

The Jedi go to the Chancellor's office with a warrant signed by the Supreme Court and the Senate.

@emergency_warrant
view-if: not warrant
subtitle: −2 political capital. Needs compelling evidence; costs precious time.
choose-if: capital >= 2 and evidence >= 7
unavailable-subtitle: Needs 2 political capital and strong evidence (7+).
on-arrival: capital -= 2; warrant = 1; arrest_mode = "warrant"; arrest_planned = 1; arrest_delay = 1

Three justices are woken in the night. By morning, the Jedi have a warrant, and the Chancellor may have had time to prepare.

@expose
view-if: evidence >= 10
subtitle: The whole Senate will know. He will have nowhere to hide, or nothing left to lose.
on-arrival: arrest_mode = "exposed"; arrest_planned = 1; evidence_public += 4; navy_loyalty += 15; senate_resolve += 2

Before the full Senate, the Caucus reveals everything. The Chancellor's allies flee from him like water from a breaking dam.

@jedi
subtitle: Speed over legitimacy.
on-arrival: arrest_mode = "jedi"; arrest_planned = 1

The Jedi go at once, alone.
